  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Triple Canopy has $324M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Triple Canopy won 66 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $4.9M. Triple Canopy obligations are down 14.6% year over year. Triple Canopy historically received larger totals in prior fiscal years: FY21 totaled $479M, FY22 totaled $382M, FY23 totaled $468M, FY24 totaled $478M, and FY25 totaled $380M. Triple Canopy work in FY2026 to date concentrates in Security Guards and Patrol Services with $282M, followed by Security Systems Services (except Locksmiths) with $23.6M, Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services with $15.6M, and Engineering Services with $3.1M. Triple Canopy receives most funding from the Department of Homeland Security at $221M, the Department of State at $91.7M, and the Department of Defense at $11.6M. The current-year totals are partial because FY2026 is fiscal year to date. This snapshot shows where Triple Canopy’s revenue is concentrated by agency and by NAICS market.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Triple Canopy's top buying agencies?",
        "body": "The Department of Homeland Security is the top buyer with $221M in FY2026 to date. The Department of State follows with $91.7M. The Department of Defense accounts for $11.6M. These three agencies make up the largest agency shares of Triple Canopy obligations in the current fiscal year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and services drive Triple Canopy's federal work?",
        "body": "Security Guards and Patrol Services is the largest market with $282M in FY2026 to date. Security Systems Services (except Locksmiths) contributes $23.6M, and Administrative Management and General Management Consulting Services contributes $15.6M. Engineering Services contributes $3.1M. These NAICS markets show where most FY2026 obligations are concentrated."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Triple Canopy make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Triple Canopy has $324M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Triple Canopy won 66 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $4.9M, and obligations are down 14.6% year over year. Triple Canopy’s work is concentrated in Security Guards and Patrol Services at $282M and in Security Systems Services at $23.6M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Triple Canopy?",
      "a": "The Department of Homeland Security buys the most from Triple Canopy, with $221M in FY2026 to date. The Department of State is the second-largest buyer at $91.7M, and the Department of Defense is the third at $11.6M."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Triple Canopy sell to the government?",
